From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jrash <johnrash@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 03:41:12 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 158/342] app_server, meson_hdmi: a mode for a display
 connected after boot

app_server picked a mode once, at start; a display connected later (a TV
switched on after the ODROID-C2, another monitor) kept that mode, even
one it doesn't list. The driver already noticed the display, read its
EDID and listed its modes, with no way to tell app_server.

A new optional accelerant hook, B_ACCELERANT_DISPLAY_CHANGE_SEMAPHORE,
gives a semaphore released when another display is connected. meson_hdmi
creates it for the calling team (app_server) and releases it when the
EDID of a display connected differs from the previous one; a display
plugged in again changes nothing. AccelerantHWInterface watches it from
a thread, reads the mode list again and tells its listeners
(DisplayChanged()); the desktop then, from its own thread (posted
AS_DISPLAY_CHANGED, as the screen manager is locked), applies the
workspace's configuration as at start: the mode stored for that monitor,
else its preferred mode, and B_SCREEN_CHANGED to the windows.

ODROID-C2, the capture stick connected after boot: at 720p without a
display it came up in the display's 1080p60; with 720p stored for that
monitor, in 720p.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
